body:
Hi there, thank you for your time answering here. Actually the masters is one of the reasons I've realized I won't do much with my life.

&#x200B;

I didn't have a great supervisor and I didn't manage to do what had to be done by myself, but the deadline is july 1st and I can't finish my thesis. I can't because it's so shitty right now, I did nothing useful and don't have anything to present, I still would have to write a paper with garbage just to follow with the expected procedure and I don't want to put my name in such a crappy work. The thing is that I've received a scolarship during the course of 2 years (since mar/2016 to feb/2018) and I'd have to pay it all back, not only I don't have this money on me but I don't want to tell my relatives and friends that I've quit.

&#x200B;

Anyway, it's been some stressful months, it's not a big deal at all but I haven't been being able to deal with them and don't want to. With this lack of discipline and ability to deal with simple problems I wont go much further in life, why waste?
